course: dictionary
lesson: 14237
title: Navel, belly button and centre
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can be easier to understand when you read the words around it. These are its context, and they leave clues. «Ravi poked his finger into his navel and giggled.» Poking a finger and giggling tells you the navel is part of the body, on the tummy.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Our town was the navel of the island, where all the roads met.» A navel is not usually a road or a town, so think about the clue: where all the roads met. A navel can mean the centre of something.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the hard word. «Our town was the centre of the island, where all the roads met.» If it still makes sense, your meaning is probably right.
fact: A navel is the small hollow or bump in the middle of your tummy.
fact: Navel is another name for your belly button.
fact: Before a baby is born, the umbilical cord carries food and oxygen from mother to baby.
fact: «Navel» can also mean the centre of something, as in «the navel of the world».
fact: A navel orange has a little bump on the end that looks like a navel.
exercise: «Ravi poked his finger into his navel and giggled.» What is a navel? | *The small hollow in the middle of your tummy | The top of a mountain | A small pair of socks | A big bone in your back
exercise: «Our town was the navel of the island, where all the roads met.» In this sentence, navel means | A bridge | *The centre | The edge or coast | A tiny bump on a tree
exercise: What is another name for your belly button? | Knee | *Navel | Ankle | Elbow
test: Why is it called a navel orange? | *It has a small bump on the end that looks like a navel | It grows on a navel tree | It is the biggest orange in the shop | It is very sweet
test: «He spent all day navel-gazing and never helped his friends.» What does navel-gazing suggest? | Looking for lost things | Looking at the stars | *Thinking too much about yourself | Running very fast
exam: Before a baby is born, what carries food and oxygen from mother to baby? | *The umbilical cord | Her milk | Her belly button | Her hands
